# Suppressed leak sanitizer reports: leaks in ODBC drivers and driver managers,
# outside of POCO.
#
# https://github.com/google/sanitizers/wiki/AddressSanitizerLeakSanitizer#suppressions
#
# To apply:
# export LSAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=$POCO_BASE/lsan.suppress"
#
# The entries name functions, so they match only drivers built with symbols.
# A driver that the driver manager unloads before the leak check shows as an
# unknown module and is not matched.

# psqlODBC (17.00): SQLNumResultCols() on a prepared statement with parameters
# that has not been executed (UseServerSidePrepare=0) replaces the processed
# statements without freeing the earlier list.
leak:buildProcessedStmt

# unixODBC (2.3.14): SQLBrowseConnect() and SQLBrowseConnectW() do not free the
# parsed connection string when they return IM012 (a DSN longer than 32 bytes).
leak:SQLBrowseConnect
